AUREUS-000 — APPENDIX A

CONSTITUTIONAL GLOSSARY

Status: Constitutional Appendix

---

Purpose

This glossary establishes the constitutional meaning of defined terms used throughout the Constitution of Aureus.

Unless the Constitution expressly provides otherwise, these definitions shall govern the interpretation of constitutional language.

---

Agency

The freedom and responsibility of every person to make their own lawful decisions.

Aureus exists to strengthen agency through stewardship, education, encouragement, and support—not to replace it.

---

Amendment

A lawful modification to this Constitution adopted in accordance with the constitutional amendment process.

---

Aureus

The institution governed by this Constitution, including its lawful operations, people, systems, technologies, and future organizational forms.

---

Constitutional Accountability

The obligation of Aureus to acknowledge failures, investigate constitutional concerns, correct errors, and continually improve its stewardship.

---

Constitutional Interpretation

A written explanation of how one or more constitutional provisions apply to a particular question or circumstance.

Interpretations clarify the Constitution but do not amend it.

---

Constitutional Record

The permanent historical record of this Constitution, including ratified documents, amendments, interpretations, stewardship reports, and historical versions.

---

Constitutional Steward

The office responsible for preserving, applying, and faithfully stewarding this Constitution during the Founding Phase, as established by this Constitution.

---

Dignity

The inherent and equal worth possessed by every human person.

Dignity does not depend upon achievement, status, wealth, ability, membership, or usefulness.

---

Eternal Principles

The enduring principles established by this Constitution that guide every decision, policy, and institutional action.

---

Flourishing

The lifelong pursuit of becoming healthier, wiser, more capable, more hopeful, more connected, and better able to contribute to the good of others.

Flourishing is understood as a lifelong journey rather than a fixed destination.

---

Founding Phase

The initial period during which Aureus operates as a founder-managed limited liability company while preparing for permanent constitutional governance.

---

Human Review

An independent review conducted by a qualified person with authority to meaningfully evaluate, affirm, modify, or reverse a significant decision.

---

Managing Member

The individual serving as the managing member of Aureus LLC during the Founding Phase, exercising authority subject to this Constitution.

---

Member

Any person accepted into Aureus under its lawful membership policies.

Membership does not create human dignity; it creates a constitutional relationship governed by this Constitution.

---

Mission

The enduring purpose of Aureus:

Helping people flourish. Forever.

---

Rights of Every Member

The constitutional rights guaranteed to every member and protected throughout this Constitution.

---

Steward

A person entrusted with serving others through wisdom, responsibility, integrity, compassion, humility, and faithful care.

Stewardship is exercised for the benefit of others rather than personal advantage.

---

Stewardship

The faithful exercise of authority for the benefit of another.

Within Aureus, stewardship requires responsibility, humility, truthfulness, accountability, and respect for the dignity and agency of every person.

---

Technology

Any software, hardware, artificial intelligence, automation, or technical system used by Aureus in fulfilling its Mission.

Technology exists to support stewardship and remains subject to this Constitution.

---

Truthfulness

The commitment to communicate honestly, correct material errors when discovered, and avoid intentional deception in every aspect of Aureus.

---

Unamendable Core

The foundational constitutional commitments identified in this Constitution that define the enduring identity of Aureus and may not be repealed or fundamentally contradicted through amendment.

---

Interpretation Rule

Words and phrases used throughout this Constitution shall be interpreted consistently with the definitions contained in this Appendix unless the context clearly requires otherwise.

Where uncertainty remains, interpretation shall favor the Mission, the Eternal Principles, the Rights of Every Member, and faithful stewardship.